. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
. *only keep Year 2018
. keep if syear==2018
(624,400 observations deleted)

. 
. *only keep children born before the interview
. keep if syear>kidgeb01 & kidgeb01>0
(12,929 observations deleted)

. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. set seed 5016

. 
. ***OUTCOME
. **gender equality measure
. * higher values refer to more egalitarian attitudes
. gen GE=plh0308_v2 
(5,714 missing values generated)

. recode GE(-99/0=.)
(2,955 changes made to GE)

. tab GE

         GE |      Freq.     Percent        Cum.
------------+-----------------------------------
          1 |        616        3.60        3.60
          2 |        851        4.97        8.57
          3 |      1,169        6.83       15.39
          4 |      2,602       15.19       30.59
          5 |      1,968       11.49       42.08
          6 |      2,693       15.73       57.80
          7 |      7,226       42.20      100.00
------------+-----------------------------------
      Total |     17,125      100.00

. 
. ***Regressor of interest
. *Having a daughter - only daughters and sons, no people without children
. gen daughter=.
(25,794 missing values generated)

. replace daughter=1 if kidsex01==2
(12,596 real changes made)

. replace daughter=0 if kidsex01==1
(13,192 real changes made)

. 
. ***drop individuals with multiple children
. *variable for second birth should be "-2 does not apply" if couples only have
>  one children
. keep if kidsex02==-2
(19,661 observations deleted)

. 
. ***Control variables
. *Year of birth
. gen birthyear=ple0010_h 
(1,345 missing values generated)

. replace birthyear=. if ple0010_h <0
(0 real changes made)

. 
. **Gender of the parent
. *binary indicator for being male
. gen male=.
(6,133 missing values generated)

. replace male=1 if sex==1
(2,712 real changes made)

. replace male=0 if sex==2
(3,421 real changes made)

. 
. **Birth year of the child
. gen birthyear_child=kidgeb01

. replace birthyear_child=. if kidgeb01<0
(0 real changes made)

. 
. **Marital status
. gen famstat=pgfamstd
(1,345 missing values generated)

. replace famstat=. if pgfamstd<0
(18 real changes made, 18 to missing)

. 
. **Education
. gen yeduc=pgbilzeit
(1,345 missing values generated)

. replace yeduc=. if pgbilzeit<0
(118 real changes made, 118 to missing)

. 
. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. /*
> Verbal description: 
> We regress the gender equality variable (GE) on having a daughter (daughter),
>  an
> interaction term between gender and having a daughter (i.daughter#i.male) and
> a set of covariates. The coefficient for daughter is the effect of interest a
> nd
> shows the effect of having a daughter for men (i.e. the interaction term)
> on gender equality attitudes.
> 
> */
. global controls "c.yeduc i.famstat i.birthyear i.birthyear_child"

. 
. reg GE  i.daughter##i.male $controls, r

